---
title: Fix audio build errors
description: Find the cause of common audio build errors, grouped by the file you're editing.
sidebar:
  order: 6
---

The build checks your audio files and stops at the first problem. It prints a line in the form `file: message`, so the file name tells you where to look. Messages about a table entry start with the kind of entry and its name, such as `Sound 'ShopBell': ...`. This page lists the common messages, grouped by the file you're editing.

## File names

| Message | Cause and fix |
| --- | --- |
| `...: this file must be named presets.xml` | Audio files use snake case names. Rename `Presets.xml` to `presets.xml`. The same message appears for `sound_effects.xml`, `drums.xml`, `sfx/envelopes.xml`, and `bank/NAME/sound_bank.xml`, each with the new name. |
| `tables merge by entry; delete entries with delete="true"` | A `.meta` file tries to delete a table file. Delete the entries with `delete="true"` instead. |
| `Instrument 'NAME': this file replaces the game's whole file, so leave the entry out instead of deleting it` | `audio/presets.xml` and `audio/drums.xml` replace the game's files whole, so `delete="true"` has nothing to remove. Leave the entry out of your copy. The message starts with `Drum` for `audio/drums.xml`. |
| `songs aren't listed in a table: ...` | Songs come from their files, not from `audio/songs.xml`. Rename each of your `.bgm` files after its song, so `<Song name="MeadowTheme" bgm="meadow.bgm"/>` becomes `audio/songs/meadow_theme.bgm`. If an entry had `bk1`, `bk2`, or `bk3`, open the song in Mamar and choose its instruments from those banks again. Then delete `audio/songs.xml`. |
| `ambient sounds aren't listed in a table: ...` | Ambient sounds come from their files, not from `audio/ambient_sounds.xml`. Rename each of your MSEQ files after its sound, so `<AmbientSound name="Rain" mseq="rain_loop"/>` becomes `audio/mseq/rain.xml`. Then delete `audio/ambient_sounds.xml`. |
| `banks aren't listed in a table: ...` | Every bank in `audio/bank/` is always loaded unless a song or the radio loads it, and the build picks each bank's slot. Delete `audio/banks.xml`. |

## Any table

| Message | Cause and fix |
| --- | --- |
| `the name must start with a letter and contain only letters, digits, and underscores` | Rename the entry. A hyphen or space isn't allowed. |
| `Sound 'NAME' is listed more than once` | The same file has two entries with one name. Keep one. |
| `Drum 'NAME': ID 2 is already used by 'OTHER'` | Two entries use the same `id`. Remove the `id` attribute from your entry to let the build pick a free one. |
| `NAME and OTHER both become SOUND_NAME` | Two names produce the same constant, such as `ShopBell` and `Shop_Bell`. Rename one. |

## Sound effects

| Message | Cause and fix |
| --- | --- |
| `OneShot: no always-loaded bank has an instrument named NAME` | The `wav` name doesn't match an instrument in an always-loaded bank. Check the spelling, and check that no song loads the sample's bank. `SetInstrument` in a sequence or in an ambient sequence gives the same message with its own name in front. Samples in a song bank aren't available to sound effects. |
| `Sound 'NAME': a sound must have exactly one of src, empty, or OneShot` | A `Sound` entry needs one of `src="sfx/..."`, `empty="true"`, or a `OneShot` child. |
| `Sound 'NAME': a sequence needs a Routing element` | An entry with `src` needs a `Routing` child. |
| `Sound 'NAME': there is no sfx/NAME.xml file in any layer` | The `src` path doesn't match a file in any layer. |
| `Sound 'NAME': ID 0009 is already used by 'MenuShowChoice'` | Two sounds use the same `id`. Remove the `id` attribute from your entry. |
| `Sound 'NAME': ID 00C5 is a direct slot, but the sound has Routing` | The `id` you pinned is a slot that can't hold a sound with `Routing`. Remove the `id` attribute. |
| `Sound 'NAME': there are no free routed sound slots` | The game has no free ID of the kind the sound needs. Delete a sound you don't use. |

## Banks and samples

| Message | Cause and fix |
| --- | --- |
| `Bank 'NAME': there is no bank/NAME/sample.wav file in any layer` | The `wav` attribute of an `Instrument` names a file that isn't in the bank's folder in any layer. Add the WAV file. |
| `Bank 'NAME': there is no bank/NAME/sound_bank.xml file in any layer` | A bank folder needs a `sound_bank.xml` file in at least one layer. |
| `the WAV file has 2 channels; only mono is supported` | Export the sample as mono. |
| `the WAV file has 24-bit samples; only 16-bit is supported` | Export the sample as 16-bit PCM. The `floating-point WAV files are not supported; use 16-bit PCM` and `the WAV file is not uncompressed PCM; use 16-bit PCM` messages have the same fix. |
| `Instrument is missing required attribute: keyBase` | Add `keyBase="4800"` to the instrument. |
| `a bank has at most 16 instruments, but there are 17` | Move instruments to another bank. |
| `the sample name NAME is also used by bank OTHER` | Rename one of the WAV files and its `wav` attributes. |
| `a bank name must be 4 characters or fewer: NAME` | Rename the bank's folder. |
| `80 banks are always loaded, but the engine loads at most 79; ...` | Delete a bank you don't need with a `.meta` file, or load it from a song instead. |
| `the layer has both this directory and NAME.bk; use only one` | A layer has both `bank/NAME/` and `bank/NAME.bk`. Delete one. |
| `Song 'NAME': bank NAME is used as an auxiliary bank, but its header is ...` | A bank that a song loads has too many instruments or envelopes. Split it into two banks. |
| `the archive is ...` | Your audio is too large for the game to load. Use shorter samples or lower sample rates. |

## Songs and ambient sounds

| Message | Cause and fix |
| --- | --- |
| `the file name must start with a lowercase letter and contain only lowercase letters, digits, and underscores` | Rename the `.bgm` or MSEQ file, such as `Meadow-Theme.bgm` to `meadow_theme.bgm`. |
| `Song 'NAME': there is no bank/NAME directory or bank/NAME.bk file in any layer` | The song loads a bank that doesn't exist. Open the song in Mamar and choose its instruments from the game's banks. |
| `the Mamar metadata at ... can't be read: ...` | The end of the `.bgm` file is damaged. Open the song in Mamar and save it again. |
| `there are more than 256 songs` | Delete a song you don't use. |
| `mseq: the radio needs all of radio_0 to radio_3, but some are missing` | The radio has four stations, and the game's code uses the radio, so it can't be removed. Restore the missing stations. |
| `the radio's stations must all play samples from one bank, but they play samples from ...` | Change the `SetInstrument` commands in `audio/mseq/radio_0.xml` to `radio_3.xml` to use samples from one bank. |
| `the radio's stations must be XML files, so the build can find the bank they play` | Replace each radio station's `.mseq` file with an `.xml` file. |
| `radio is the name of the radio; rename the file` | `audio/mseq/radio.xml` would give a second `AMBIENT_RADIO`. Rename the file. |
| `command 12, EndLoop: loop 0 repeats forever without a Delay` | Add a `Delay` inside the loop in the MSEQ file. |

## Compiler errors after a deletion

If you delete an entry that C code or an EVT script still uses, the audio build succeeds but the compiler reports that the constant is undeclared:

```text
error: 'SONG_TOAD_TOWN' undeclared (first use in this function)
```

Search your code for the constant that the error names, and remove or change each use.
